{
  "id": "lakehouse",
  "name": "Lakehouse (Iceberg / Delta)",
  "profile": "rust-native",
  "upstream": "exasol-labs/lakehouse-engine-rs",
  "family": "lakehouse",
  "adapter": {
    "version": "0.57.3",
    "license": "MIT",
    "bundle": "tar.gz",
    "member": "udf/liblakehouse_engine.so",
    "arch": {
      "aarch64": {
        "asset": "lakehouse-engine-aarch64.tar.gz",
        "url": "https://github.com/exasol-labs/lakehouse-engine-rs/releases/download/v0.57.3/lakehouse-engine-aarch64.tar.gz",
        "size": 61428965,
        "sha256": "c90cecd55f6a1e034717cffd0af732976f7419a8d778887cae11d8b905462791",
        "member_size": 203873112,
        "member_sha256": "6f34346413c2ea1c49b62f1c36e7f5aca0663e8c42b771e55b9939a690718197"
      },
      "x86_64": {
        "asset": "lakehouse-engine.tar.gz",
        "url": "https://github.com/exasol-labs/lakehouse-engine-rs/releases/download/v0.57.3/lakehouse-engine.tar.gz",
        "size": 59188013,
        "sha256": "7eb321de789b75edb45e6af26b7d710a4c5f56265808c4515e5e8bb58bdbd5c1",
        "member_size": 218989960,
        "member_sha256": "f058464f1d021dcbcfae63a5528f9aec92d8c38eb02eef434a2c0315ff57b05d"
      }
    }
  },
  "driver": null,
  "etl": null,
  "shared_adapter": "LAKEHOUSE_ADAPTER",
  "shared_by": "lakehouse source",
  "companions": [
    {
      "name": "LAKEHOUSE_SCAN",
      "language": "RUST",
      "type": "SCALAR",
      "signature": "(common VARCHAR(2000000), files VARCHAR(2000000)) EMITS (...)"
    },
    {
      "name": "LAKEHOUSE_DISTRIBUTE_FILES",
      "language": "LUA",
      "type": "SET",
      "signature": "(files VARCHAR(2000000)) EMITS (files VARCHAR(2000000))",
      "body": "function run(ctx)\n    repeat\n        ctx.emit(ctx.files)\n    until not ctx.next()\nend"
    },
    {
      "name": "LAKEHOUSE_VERSION",
      "language": "RUST",
      "type": "SCALAR",
      "signature": "() RETURNS VARCHAR(100)"
    }
  ],
  "version_script": "LAKEHOUSE_VERSION",
  "_settings_comment": [
    "One connector, three settings. catalog and files pick the combination; login",
    "applies to the catalogs that sign in (Iceberg REST, Unity). files.valid lists",
    "the files values each catalog takes, files.default the one an omitted files",
    "takes (none: by the folder path's scheme, see plan.py). An input's `when`",
    "names the setting values it is asked for (every key must match; a key left",
    "out matches any value). variants are the catalog's own connector fields,",
    "laid over this document once the combination is known (plan.specialize)."
  ],
  "settings": {
    "catalog": {
      "label": "Catalog",
      "choices": [
        {
          "value": "iceberg-rest",
          "label": "Iceberg REST catalog"
        },
        {
          "value": "unity",
          "label": "Unity Catalog"
        },
        {
          "value": "glue",
          "label": "AWS Glue"
        },
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "No catalog - Parquet files in a folder"
        }
      ],
      "infer": {
        "catalog_url": "iceberg-rest",
        "warehouse": "iceberg-rest",
        "workspace_url": "unity",
        "database": "glue",
        "catalog_id": "glue",
        "path": "none"
      }
    },
    "files": {
      "label": "Files",
      "choices": [
        {
          "value": "vended",
          "label": "Let the catalog give access"
        },
        {
          "value": "s3",
          "label": "Amazon S3 / S3-compatible"
        },
        {
          "value": "azure",
          "label": "Azure ADLS Gen2"
        },
        {
          "value": "gcs",
          "label": "Google Cloud Storage - not supported yet",
          "disabled": true
        }
      ],
      "valid": {
        "iceberg-rest": [
          "vended",
          "s3",
          "azure"
        ],
        "unity": [
          "vended",
          "s3",
          "azure"
        ],
        "glue": [
          "s3"
        ],
        "none": [
          "s3",
          "azure"
        ]
      },
      "default": {
        "iceberg-rest": "vended",
        "unity": "vended",
        "glue": "s3",
        "none": "s3"
      }
    },
    "login": {
      "label": "Catalog login",
      "choices": [
        {
          "value": "token",
          "label": "Token"
        },
        {
          "value": "oauth",
          "label": "OAuth client (ID + secret)"
        }
      ],
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "iceberg-rest",
          "unity"
        ]
      },
      "default": "token"
    }
  },
  "inputs": [
    {
      "name": "catalog_url",
      "label": "Catalog URL",
      "kind": "catalog-url",
      "required": true,
      "prompt": "Catalog URL (https://host[:port][/path]; http only for this computer or a private network)",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "iceberg-rest"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "warehouse",
      "label": "Warehouse (catalog name)",
      "kind": "warehouse",
      "required": true,
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "iceberg-rest"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "namespace",
      "label": "Namespace",
      "kind": "iceberg-namespace",
      "required": true,
      "prompt": "Namespace (one namespace is one virtual schema)",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "iceberg-rest"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "workspace_url",
      "label": "Workspace URL",
      "kind": "https-url",
      "required": true,
      "prompt": "Workspace URL (https://..., e.g. https://dbc-1234.cloud.databricks.com)",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "unity"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "namespace",
      "label": "Catalog.schema",
      "kind": "unity-namespace",
      "required": true,
      "prompt": "Catalog.schema (e.g. main.sales; one schema is one virtual schema)",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "unity"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "region",
      "label": "AWS region",
      "kind": "aws-region",
      "required": true,
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "glue"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "database",
      "label": "Glue database",
      "kind": "glue-database",
      "required": true,
      "prompt": "Glue database (one database is one virtual schema)",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "glue"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "access_key_id",
      "label": "Access key ID",
      "kind": "aws-key-id",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "glue"
        ]
      },
      "prompt": "Access key ID (Enter if the credential file - the JSON aws iam create-access-key prints - holds it)"
    },
    {
      "name": "secret",
      "label": "Secret access key",
      "kind": "secret",
      "required": true,
      "role": "aws",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "glue"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "catalog_id",
      "label": "Glue catalog ID",
      "kind": "aws-account-id",
      "prompt": "Glue catalog ID (optional: the 12-digit account that owns the catalog, when it is not yours)",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "glue"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "path",
      "label": "Folder path",
      "kind": "storage-path",
      "required": true,
      "prompt": "Folder path (s3://bucket/prefix/)",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "none"
        ],
        "files": [
          "s3"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "path",
      "label": "Folder path",
      "kind": "storage-path",
      "required": true,
      "prompt": "Folder path (abfss://container@account.dfs.core.windows.net/prefix/)",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "none"
        ],
        "files": [
          "azure"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "secret",
      "label": "Catalog token",
      "kind": "secret",
      "required": true,
      "role": "token",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "iceberg-rest"
        ],
        "login": [
          "token"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "secret",
      "label": "Databricks token",
      "kind": "secret",
      "required": true,
      "role": "token",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "unity"
        ],
        "login": [
          "token"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "client_id",
      "label": "Client ID",
      "kind": "oauth-client-id",
      "required": true,
      "when": {
        "login": [
          "oauth"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "secret",
      "label": "Client secret",
      "kind": "secret",
      "required": true,
      "role": "client_secret",
      "when": {
        "login": [
          "oauth"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "token_endpoint",
      "label": "Token endpoint",
      "kind": "catalog-url",
      "prompt": "Token endpoint (optional: Enter for the catalog's own)",
      "when": {
        "login": [
          "oauth"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "scope",
      "label": "Scope",
      "kind": "oauth-scope",
      "prompt": "Scope (optional, e.g. PRINCIPAL_ROLE:ALL)",
      "when": {
        "login": [
          "oauth"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "region",
      "label": "AWS region",
      "kind": "aws-region",
      "prompt": "AWS region (optional; only if the files are on S3)",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "iceberg-rest",
          "unity"
        ],
        "files": [
          "vended"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "region",
      "label": "AWS region",
      "kind": "storage-region",
      "required": true,
      "prompt": "AWS region (the bucket's; an S3-compatible store such as MinIO usually answers to us-east-1)",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "iceberg-rest",
          "unity",
          "none"
        ],
        "files": [
          "s3"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "access_key_id",
      "label": "Access key ID",
      "kind": "access-key",
      "required": true,
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "iceberg-rest",
          "unity"
        ],
        "files": [
          "s3"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "access_key_id",
      "label": "Access key ID",
      "kind": "access-key",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "none"
        ],
        "files": [
          "s3"
        ]
      },
      "prompt": "Access key ID (Enter if the credential file - the JSON aws iam create-access-key prints - holds it)"
    },
    {
      "name": "storage_secret",
      "label": "Secret access key",
      "kind": "secret",
      "required": true,
      "role": "storage",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "iceberg-rest",
          "unity"
        ],
        "files": [
          "s3"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "secret",
      "label": "Secret access key",
      "kind": "secret",
      "required": true,
      "role": "storage",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "none"
        ],
        "files": [
          "s3"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "endpoint",
      "label": "Endpoint",
      "kind": "endpoint-url",
      "prompt": "Endpoint (S3-compatible store, optional: e.g. https://minio.example.com:9000)",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "iceberg-rest",
          "unity",
          "none"
        ],
        "files": [
          "s3"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "account_name",
      "label": "Azure storage account",
      "kind": "azure-account",
      "required": true,
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "iceberg-rest",
          "unity"
        ],
        "files": [
          "azure"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "storage_secret",
      "label": "Account key or SAS",
      "kind": "secret",
      "required": true,
      "role": "storage",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "iceberg-rest",
          "unity"
        ],
        "files": [
          "azure"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "secret",
      "label": "Account key or SAS",
      "kind": "secret",
      "required": true,
      "role": "storage",
      "when": {
        "catalog": [
          "none"
        ],
        "files": [
          "azure"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variants": {
    "iceberg-rest": {
      "host_from": "catalog_url",
      "url": "{catalog_url}",
      "vs_properties": {
        "NAMESPACE": "{namespace}"
      },
      "paste": {
        "style": "catalog",
        "input": "catalog_url",
        "forms": [
          "https://<catalog-host>[:port][/path]"
        ]
      }
    },
    "unity": {
      "host_from": "workspace_url",
      "url": "{workspace_url}",
      "vs_properties": {
        "CATALOG_KIND": "UNITY_CATALOG",
        "NAMESPACE": "{namespace}"
      },
      "paste": {
        "style": "catalog",
        "input": "workspace_url",
        "forms": [
          "https://<workspace-host>"
        ]
      }
    },
    "glue": {
      "host": "glue.{region}.amazonaws.com",
      "url": "https://glue.{region}.amazonaws.com",
      "vs_properties": {
        "CATALOG_KIND": "GLUE",
        "NAMESPACE": "{database}"
      },
      "paste": {
        "style": "glue",
        "forms": [
          "https://glue.<region>.amazonaws.com",
          "arn:aws:glue:<region>:<account>:database/<name>"
        ]
      }
    },
    "none": {
      "url": "{path}",
      "vs_properties": {
        "CATALOG_KIND": "DIRECT_STORAGE"
      },
      "paste": {
        "style": "lakehouse",
        "forms": [
          "s3://<bucket>/<prefix>/",
          "abfss://<container>@<account>.dfs.core.windows.net/<prefix>/"
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "paste": {
    "style": "lakehouse",
    "forms": [
      "https://<catalog-host>[:port][/path] (Iceberg REST)",
      "https://<workspace-host> (Unity Catalog)",
      "arn:aws:glue:<region>:<account>:database/<name>",
      "s3://<bucket>/<prefix>/",
      "abfss://<container>@<account>.dfs.core.windows.net/<prefix>/"
    ]
  },
  "auth": "lakehouse",
  "credential": "lakehouse",
  "connection_property": "CATALOG_CONNECTION",
  "access": "read on the catalog's namespace (list and load its tables) and read on the table files: s3:ListBucket and s3:GetObject, or Storage Blob Data Reader on the container; for Glue also glue:GetDatabase, GetTables, GetTable and GetPartitions; for Unity Catalog USE CATALOG, USE SCHEMA, SELECT and EXTERNAL USE SCHEMA",
  "auth_hint": "the catalog login is a token (or an OAuth client's ID and secret) the catalog accepts; the storage secret, when the files are not vended, is the S3 secret key or the Azure account key or SAS",
  "vs_when_http": {
    "ALLOW_HTTP": "true"
  },
  "tips": [
    "Names arrive in upper case (ORDERS, ORDER_ID): no quotes needed.",
    "One namespace (Glue: database; Unity: catalog.schema; no catalog: folder) is one virtual schema: connect again with another --name for the next one."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "exasol-labs' lakehouse-engine-rs runs Apache DataFusion inside the Rust language container (the same 0.33.0 container MongoDB uses). One pinned build, one LAKEHOUSE_ADAPTER and its companion scripts in EXAKIT_VS serve every lakehouse source, whatever its catalog.",
    "The CONNECTION goes TO the catalog's address (Iceberg REST: the catalog URL; Unity: the workspace URL; Glue: https://glue.<region>.amazonaws.com; no catalog: the folder path) with an empty user; its password is JSON the kit writes from the catalog login and the files' access. CATALOG_KIND is UNITY_CATALOG, GLUE or DIRECT_STORAGE (absent for Iceberg REST).",
    "Two secrets at most: the catalog's (a token or an OAuth client secret; for Glue the AWS secret key; with no catalog the storage secret) on --password-file or --password-stdin, and the storage secret (S3 secret key, Azure account key or SAS) on --storage-secret-file, or asked hidden. Neither is ever taken as an argument.",
    "The release is a .tar.gz pinned per CPU; the .so inside it is pinned too, and staged only when both match. Iceberg deletes are applied (positional and deletion vectors); equality deletes, ORC and Avro are refused by name.",
    "https by default. Plain http is accepted only when typed, and only towards this computer or a private network; the virtual schema then carries ALLOW_HTTP. localhost is refused: inside the database it is the database itself."
  ]
}
